From 8b9a799390e37d3cca1272c2f5bc24cf6d9acba0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:57:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: correct pipeline metrics, entrypoint and docs after repo
 review

- JobRepository.salvar now returns "salva", "duplicada" or "erro".
  It returned None, so PipelineService counted every job as an error.
  A UNIQUE violation on link is now treated as a duplicate.
- main.py ended with a stray `ls` (NameError on every run) and bypassed
  PipelineService. It now runs the full pipeline and exits 1 on failure.
- PipelineService fails when zero jobs are collected instead of
  reporting success.
- Replace print() with the project logger in the repository, collector,
  base scraper and dashboard service.
- Stop tracking 31 .pyc files that .gitignore already excluded.
- dashboard.yml publishes only index.html (not the whole repo), runs only
  when it changes, and drops the debug step.
- Replace Cloud Run/Secret Manager references with Render.
- README: real file tree, real test counts (98), dashboard path
  (index.html), DB_NAME matching .env.example, and how the public
  dashboard is actually updated.
- Add tests for JobRepository and PipelineService/main.

